    }
</script>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl40_divContent"><h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">School Board Policies</h2>
<p>The School Board of Polk County determines and adopts lawful policies and programs that are deemed necessary for the efficient operation and general improvement of the school district. The School Board also adopts rules and regulations to supplement those prescribed by the State Board of Education that will contribute to an orderly and efficient operation of the school district.</p>
<p><a href="https://go.neola.com/polk-fl/policy" target="_blank" title="External Link to Neola">View School Board Policies</a></p></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl43_divContent"><h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">Student Nutrition</h2>
<p style="margin-top: 20px;">For additional information regarding Special Dietary Needs and Diet Modification Forms, please visit our <a href="https://www.polkschoolsfl.com/studentsandparents/nutrition" title="Link to the school nutrition webpage">School Nutrition page</a>.</p></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl46_divContent"><div id="studentprogressionplan">
<h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">Student Progression Plan</h2>
<p>The Student Progression Plan for Polk County Public Schools presents the School Board rule and administrative procedures required for implementing state legislative and local School Board pupil progression requirements. Specific criteria have been set in the Student Progression Plan. The plan is designed to indicate what actions will be taken during the school year to assist the student. Particular emphasis is placed upon the pupil’s mastery of basic skills before he/she is promoted.</p>
<a href="/UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/Image/Quick Links/Student Progression/25-26 Student Progression Planv4.pdf" target="_self" title="Link to the Student Progression Plan Document">2025-26 Student Progression Plan (PDF)</a></div></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl49_divContent"><h2 style="margin-top:50px;">Transportation and Support Services</h2>
<ul>
    <li><a href="/cms/One.aspx?portalId=3007402&amp;pageId=3309351" target="_self" title="Internal Link to the Transportation Page">Rules for Riding the bus, Pupil Transportation FAQ's and Field Trip Information links</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.polkschoolsfl.com/UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/File/Students%20and%20Parents/Policies%20Procedures%20and%20Forms/Form%208660F1%20POV%20Approval.pdf" title="Form">Approved Volunteers Application to Transport Students in Privately Owned Vehicles</a></li>
</ul></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl52_divContent"><h2 id="WirelessPolicy" style="margin-top:50px;">Wireless Communication Device Policy</h2>
<p>Our goal is to create a safe environment, conducive to learning, and free from distractions that hinder the learning process. PCPS has established the following practices in line with HB 1105 and District policy 5136-Wireless Communication Devices as stated in the Code of Student Conduct.</p></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div>
<style type="text/css">
    .disabledIco {
        color: lightgrey;
    }
</style>
<div id="tabPortlet_206898" data-clientId="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl55" class="PO-wrapper PO-tabAccordion">
    
    
    <div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl55_upPanel">
	
            <div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl55_divTabs" role="region" style="width:100%;" class="TA-accordionMode" portlet="accordion" aria-label="Accordion Portlet">
                
            </div>
        
</div>
    
    <label for="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl55_divTabEdit" aria-hidden="true"  Style="display: none">tab visible</label>
    <input name="ctl00$ContentPlaceHolder1$ctl55$divTabEdit" type="text" value="True" id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl55_divTabEdit" class="divTabEdit" style="display: none" />
    
</div>

<script type="text/javascript">
    
	$(document).ready(function () {
		var logConsole = function (str) {
			console.log(str);
		};
		if ($('#tabPortlet_206898 .divTabEdit').val() == "True") {
			var isModern = ('True');
			if (isModern.toLowerCase() == "true") {
				var tabObj = $('#tabPortlet_206898 ');
				var tabM = $('#ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl55_divTabs').attr('portlet') == 'tab';

				function activate() {
					$(tabObj).scrollingTabs({
						tabs: [{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl55_divTabs_0","title":"Wireless Communication Device Policy for Students","content":"<p>House Bill 1105 states that all elementary and middle school students are <strong><em>PROHIBITED</em></strong> from using wireless communication devices during the school day.  Students are permitted to have a wireless device in their possession at school, however the device must remain out of sight and powered off during the school day. </p>\n<p>House Bill 1105 states that all high school students are&nbsp;<strong><em>PROHIBITED</em></strong>&nbsp;from using wireless communication devices during instructional time, unless permitted by the teacher for educational purposes only.&nbsp; Students are permitted to have a wireless device in their possession at school, however the device must remain out of sight and powered off during the school day.&nbsp; School Administration will adopt policies addressing locations within the school where a high school student can use their device when granted permission.</p>\n<p>Wireless communication device usage is a <em><strong>privilege</strong></em> that may be <strong><em>forfeited</em></strong> by any student who fails to abide by the terms of the school and/or District policy or abuses the privilege.</p>\n<p><b>The following consequences will apply for a student using a cellphone during restricted times:</b></p>\n<p><b>Classroom Consequences:</b></p>\n<ul>\n    <li>1st Infraction Teacher will contact home to notify of the issue and submit a minor infraction in Focus.</li>\n    <li>2nd Infraction – Teacher will contact home to notify of the issue and submit a minor infraction in Focus.</li>\n    <li>3rd Infraction - Teacher will contact home to notify of the issue and submit a minor infraction in Focus.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>****After the 3rd minor, a referral&nbsp;will be generated. Minors are cumulative throughout ALL teachers/staff. ****</strong></p>\n<div><b>Administrative Consequences (begin with 4th Infraction):</b></div>\n<ul>\n    <li>4th Infraction – Teacher will call for administration to confiscate the device. Student will walk with administrator to discipline office.&nbsp; Administrator will complete the confiscation form and put device with form in the locked box. Administrator will contact the parent. The student will be issued 1 day of In-School-Suspension. Student will pick up the phone at the end of the school day. (Document in Focus/PCD)</li>\n    <li>5th Infraction – Teacher will call for administration to confiscate the device. Student will walk with administrator to discipline office.&nbsp; Admin will complete the confiscation form and put device with form in the locked box. Admin will contact the parent and label the referral description as “Gross Insubordination” and issue the student 3 days of in-school suspension.&nbsp; Parent will pick up the device at the end of school day. (Document in Focus/PCD)</li>\n    <li>6th Infraction – Teacher will call for administration to confiscate the device. Student will walk with administrator to discipline office.&nbsp; Admin will complete the confiscation form and put device with form in the locked box. Admin will contact the parent and label the referral description as “Gross Insubordination” and issue the student 3 days of out -of-school suspension.&nbsp; Parent will pick up the device at the end of school day. (Document in Focus/PCD)</li>\n    <li>7th Infraction – Teacher will call for administration to confiscate the device. Student will walk with administrator to discipline office.&nbsp; Admin will complete the confiscation form and put device with form in the locked box.&nbsp; Admin will contact the parent and label the referral description as “Gross Insubordination” and issue the student 5 days of out -of-school suspension. Parent will pick up the device at the end of school day. (Document in Focus/PCD) The student will lose the privilege of having a cellphone on campus for 9 weeks (45 school days).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Subsequent Infractions – Following progressive discipline, the following actions will be taken for any subsequent violations:</b></p>\n<ul>\n    <li>7 days of out-of-school suspension</li>\n    <li>10 days of out-of-school suspension</li>\n    <li>Referral to alternative education setting</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Serious infractions can result in students immediately losing the privilege to carry a cellphone on campus. </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Examples of this include, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n    <li>Refusing to give the device to a school administration who request it.</li>\n    <li>Communicating messages in any manner that reasonably creates an impression of threatening, humiliating, intimidating, or harassing of other students.</li>\n    <li>Distributing messages depicting nudity or acts of a sexual nature to include sexting.</li>\n    <li>Utilization of camera/audio recordings at any time where a reasonable expectation of personal privacy exists.</li>\n    <li>Posting harmful material or making threats against students and/or any members of the school community.</li>\n    <li>Recording or sharing recordings of fights or other major campus disruptions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Students are personally and solely responsible for the care and security of their cellphone. The Board and school assume no responsibility for theft, loss, damage to, or misuse/unauthorized use of WCDs brought onto campus. Families who need to get in touch with their child during the school day should call the school office.</p>\n<p>If you have any questions or concerns, please do not hesitate to contact the school directly. Thank you for your continued support and cooperation.</p>","active":true,"disabled":false}],// required,
						propPaneId: 'paneId', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propTitle: 'title', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propActive: 'active', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
